The `get` method of the view takes two parameters: `request`, which represents the HTTP request being made by the user, and `username`, which contains the value of the username parameter in the URL.

Inside the `get` method, the `render` function is called with the name of the template file (`'hello.html'`), as well as a dictionary containing the value of the `username` variable. The `render` function returns a response object that contains the rendered template and any other necessary data.

When the user visits the URL `/hello/<username>`, Django will call the `get` method of the `HelloView` class with the value of `<username>` as an argument, and return the rendered template to the user. The template will display the contents of the `hello.html` file, as well as the value of the `username` variable."]

